<p>President Trump signed a new U.S. national counterterrorism strategy that makes eliminating drug cartels in the Western Hemisphere the administration’s top priority, according to the White House and Sebastian Gorka, the president’s counterterrorism adviser. The 16-page document also identifies “legacy Islamist terrorists” and “violent left-wing extremists, including anarchists and anti-fascists” as principal threats, and Gorka said the administration would use constitutionally available tools against groups that advocate or use violence for political purposes. The strategy describes Europe as both a terrorism target and an “incubator” of terrorist threats, saying mass migration, open borders and “globalist ideals” allow hostile groups to exploit U.S. allies. CBS News reported that the strategy calls for the United States to press allies to bolster counterterrorism efforts. Gorka presented the strategy to reporters on Wednesday, after CBS News reported that Trump signed it on Tuesday.</p><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Cartel focus: The strategy seeks to disrupt cartel operations and stop traffickers from moving drugs or people across the U.S. border, according to Gorka and accounts of the White House plan.</li><li>Domestic targets: Semafor said designating antifa as a terrorist organization is unusual for an ostensibly U.S.-based movement without centralized leadership.</li><li>State sponsors: Gorka said the plan would also apply to state sponsors of extremist groups and governments carrying out lethal plots on U.S. soil or against Americans anywhere.</li><li>Policy shift: Le Temps said the document breaks from the Biden administration, which had identified far-right groups, especially white supremacist groups, as a major U.S. threat.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Sebastian Gorka: Gorka mentioned the assassination of Turning Point USA founder Charlie Kirk while discussing political violence; Semafor said prosecutors argue the accused killer targeted Kirk because of the conservative activist’s politics. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/06/2026/trump-administration-focuses-on-left-wing-groups-in-new-counterterrorism-plan'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>White House strategy: The document says the United States faces “new categories and combinations of violent actors” that make established counterterrorism methods insufficient or obsolete. (<a href='https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/us/2026/05/06/us-counter-terrorism-strategy-calls-cartels-islamist-groups-and-left-wing-violence-top-threats/'>The National</a>)</li><li>Trump administration: The Straits Times said the strategy is driven by the principle that “America is our homeland and must be protected.” (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-signs-new-counterterrorism-strategy-that-focuses-on-hemispheric-threats'>The Straits Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/06/2026/trump-administration-focuses-on-left-wing-groups-in-new-counterterrorism-plan'>Left-wing groups targeted in new Trump counterterrorism plan</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/05/07/g-s1-120655/trump-counterterrorism-western-hemisphere'>Trump&#x27;s counterterrorism strategy makes targeting drug cartels the top priority</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/trump-signs-new-counterterrorism-strategy-that-focuses-on-hemispheric-threats'>Trump signs new counterterrorism strategy that focuses on hemispheric threats, Antifa</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/07/new-trump-counterterrorism-strategy-targets-europe-terrorism-migration'>US says migration has made Europe an ‘incubator’ for terrorism in new counter-terrorism strategy</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639551-europe-nato-terror-incubators/'>US blasts ‘wealthy NATO allies’ as terror incubators</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://n